  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Calm, dense operations console",
    "overview": "Graphite surfaces, teal selection, restrained state colors, IBM Plex Sans and Mono, fine rules and dense readable rows. The interface follows the user's Linear-style dark operations-console direction: calm, dense, one accent color. Technical reviewers can inspect the same working evidence that operators use.\n\nCompact plain titles keep the working interface near the top. Agents are the protagonist and their shared city stays visible beside them on operational screens; reading and evaluation screens use the same material language without imitating the map layout. Color communicates state, selection or data. The confirmed anti-references are decorative heroes, oversized marketing headlines, split-color or gradient headline text, purple gradients, Inter-everywhere and nested cards.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Local IBM Plex fonts, tabular operational values and explicit technical identifiers.",
      "Flat graphite surfaces separated by fine rules; teal marks actions and selection.",
      "Readable rows, plain labels, visible focus and progressive disclosure of evidence.",
      "Runtime data remains inspectable; missing history and measurements remain explicit."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "One Accent",
        "body": "Teal identifies primary action, selection and observed activity. Positive, negative, warning and information colors carry operational meaning; they are not alternate brand accents.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "Compact Title",
        "body": "Start with a plain workspace title and the working interface. Do not add a display headline, decorative hero or slogan.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "Flat Surface",
        "body": "Separate working areas with tonal changes and fine rules. Keep ordinary panels and rows shadowless; reserve the small ambient shadow for map overlays.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep simulation setup separate from the operation view where that separation is implemented.",
      "Do preserve distinct entity names, technical IDs and role labels when inspecting agents.",
      "Do use SVG symbols with text labels and state descriptions; color alone must not carry meaning.",
      "Do label the history window, units, simulation clock and session state; render curves only from observed samples.",
      "Do keep unavailable metrics, synthetic fixtures, retained-evidence limits and stale-source caveats visible.",
      "Do retain keyboard focus, reduced-motion behavior, local overflow containers and mobile disclosure controls."
    ],
